Validated with @qdequele and @gmourier 

@meilisearch/docs-team in v0.27.0, a non-customizable hard limit will be put to the search engine.
This limit will be `1000` and will only be applied to the `GET/POST /indexes/:uid/search` route. Calling the endpoint, Meilisearch will not return more than 1000 documents. This limit is a security fix to avoid the Meilisearch DB to be scrapped. If the Meilisearch users still want to scrap their own DB to retrieve all their documents, the `GET /indexes/:uid/documents` is still usable since the limit is not applied to this route.
